    {
      "name": "Oldenborn",
      "type": "species",
      "img": "art/bbttcc/asli-icons/oldborne_sky.webp",
      "system": {
        "category": "ancestry",
        "source": {
          "custom": "Bad Eden",
          "rules": "2024",
          "revision": 2,
          "book": "",
          "license": ""
        },
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "\n<p><strong>Oldenborn.</strong></p><p><em>“You are not an elf. You are the memory of a place that learned to walk again.”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Dream-Flesh.</strong> You do not sleep. When you rest, you drift into Yesod—symbolic memory-space—unless you choose otherwise. You are immune to magical sleep, and you can always tell when a dream, illusion, or constructed reality is present.</p>\n<p><strong>Old Memory, Old Paths.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on checks to interpret ruins, follow ley-lines, identify altered terrain, and sense metaphysical instability. You always know if a place feels <em>remembered</em>, <em>abandoned</em>, or <em>contested</em> (the GM answers vaguely).</p>\n<p><strong>Veil-Sight.</strong> You perceive the <em>presence</em> of spirits, ghosts, Spark echoes, and noospheric constructs. This grants awareness, not perfect sight.</p>\n<p><strong>You Are Remembered.</strong> When you first meet a community, the GM chooses (or rolls) whether you are met with reverence, fear, or familiarity. It’s never neutral.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
