    {
      "name": "Oldenborn (Rustland Scavenger): Ruin-Sense",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-teal.webp",
      "system": {
        "category": "feature",
        "source": {
          "custom": "Bad Eden",
          "rules": "2024",
          "revision": 2,
          "book": "",
          "license": ""
        },
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "\n<p><em>“The dead cities are not silent. They are mid-sentence.”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Ruin-Sense.</strong> When you spend 10 minutes examining a broken or ruined object, you can ask the GM one of: <em>What was its last use? Who broke it? What does it still want?</em> The answer is at least one truth.</p>\n<p><strong>Scavenger’s Eye (1/Soma Break).</strong> Spend 10 minutes searching a rubble pile, gutted building, or wreckage of any kind. You recover one minor useful item — the GM picks from a short list of plausible salvage (a half-charged battery, a length of usable wire, a sealed container of clean water, a still-edible ration, a tool of one trade). It is what the place actually had.</p>\n<p><strong>Toxic-Lung Filters.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on checks against airborne poisons, toxic gas, and rad-dust. You can hold your breath for 10 minutes.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
